0..56 Comment "/// This source states univalence for the user universe."
57..99 Comment "/// It follows the HoTT book\'s § 2.10 and"
100..157 Comment "/// cubical Agda\'s `Cubical/Foundations/Univalence.agda`."
158..161 Comment "///"
162..221 Comment "/// A bi-invertible map makes a path between its two types."
222..268 Comment "/// Transport along that path applies the map."
269..272 Comment "///"
273..322 Comment "/// The checker admits `ua` from the record laws."
323..372 Comment "/// The kernel replays the two owed inverse laws."
373..444 Comment "/// `ua` admits any two codes, also two variables, or a path type and a"
445..509 Comment "/// presented type, which no finite round-trip coverage reaches."
510..513 Comment "///"
514..556 Comment "/// - see: #650 — `oneBack`, `idtoequiv`"
557..588 Comment "/// - see: #695 — `idtoequiv`"
589..620 Comment "/// - see: #698 — `idtoequiv`"
621..664 Comment "/// - see: #1979 — `loopsAreTheirWinding`"
665..692 Comment "/// - see: #520 — `uaEta`"
693..725 Comment "/// - see: #656 — `univalence`"
726..797 Comment "// The circle, the presented integers, the winding number and spinning."
